<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murano</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Murano is a group of islands in the Venetian lagoon, about 1.5 kilometres north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. In 1291 the republic ordered glassmakers to move their furnaces there, partly to reduce the risk of fire in the city, and Murano became the centre of Venetian glass-making, famous for its crystal glass, mirrors and coloured glass. Its glassworkers were long forbidden to leave the republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/murano.jpg" alt="Murano" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wittylama · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murano_sunset.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
